    "stop_reason": "success",
    "result_text": "`AcceptanceTest` is the only test class, and the full build is green.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the `salutation` feature following the existing derived-attribute conventions in this Spring Boot app.\n\n**What the spec required:** the create request may include a `title` (MR/MRS/MS/DR); the API returns `salutation` = `title + ' ' + lastName`, or just `lastName` when no title is given.\n\n**Changes:**\n\n1. **`src/main/resources/openapi.yml`** \u2014 added `title` (optional input string) to the `OwnerFields` schema and `salutation` (read-only) to the `Owner` schema. These regenerate the `OwnerFieldsDto`/`OwnerDto` at build time; MapStruct then wires them automatically by property name.\n\n2. **`OwnerDerivations.java`** \u2014 added a pure `salutation(title, lastName)` derivation matching the file's stateless style (returns bare `lastName` for a null/blank title, else `title + \" \" + lastName`).\n\n3. **`Owner.java`** \u2014 added the persistent `title` column with getter/setter, plus a `@Transient getSalutation()` that delegates to `OwnerDerivations`, mirroring the other derived getters (`getLocality`, `getTimezone`, etc.).\n\n4. **DB schemas** \u2014 added a `title` column to the `owners` table in all four dialects (hsqldb \u2014 used by tests \u2014 plus h2, mysql, postgres) so the persisted title survives the create\u2192re-fetch round trip the test exercises.\n\nI kept `title` as a plain string rather than an OpenAPI enum specifically to avoid enum\u2194String mapping complexity in MapStruct; the allowed values are documented in the field description.\n\n**Result:** `AcceptanceTest.coreComposesSalutation` (posts `title=DR`, `lastName=who`, expects `$.salutation == \"DR who\"`) passes, and the full suite is `BUILD SUCCESS` (1 test, 0 failures).",
